{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Thus shall be done for the one ox.</b> We find that the Torah did not distinguish between the libations of a calf and the libations of an ox." "<b>Or for the one ram.</b> Why is this stated? Since we find that the Torah distinguished between the libations of a yearling and the libations of a two-year-old, so too it should distinguish between the libations of a young sheep and the libations of a ewe. Therefore Scripture says <b>'or for the ram.'</b> <b>'Or for a sheep'</b> — to teach you that you shall not distinguish between the libations of a young sheep and the libations of a ewe. <b>'Among lambs or among goats'</b> — why is this stated? Since we find that the Torah distinguished between the libations of lambs and the libations of a ram, so too it should distinguish between the libations of a kid and the libations of a he-goat. Therefore Scripture says <b>'among lambs or among goats'</b> — it draws an analogy between the largest among the goats and the smallest among the lambs: just as this one has three log, so too that one has three log."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:04.788241901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}